    {
      "id": 234125,
      "name": "Trajector",
      "username": "Trajector",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2020-11-12T20:49:41.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Can I also appreciate how Paul literally knows rocket science?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Haha, yeah, I loved that he jumped straight to hydrazine as the nasty chemical. That stuff is terrible to be around. The other thing that I would have thought of right away is hydrofluoric acid - and that gets used in biotech/nanotech stuff, which seems relevant. The building next to mine in grad school had HF, and if anyone ever spilled a drop, they had to evacuate the whole place.</p>\n<p>I have to say, I’m the weird Trekkie who went back and watched DS9, and really doesn’t think that it lives up to the hype. But I get why people point to it. It was fun to hear Paul expound on his take.</p>",
